.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt ROOK-CONFIG 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rook-config
.Nd rook's configuration: the environment graph and the program that emits it
.Sh DESCRIPTION
rook's configuration is a
.Em graph
of nodes in
.Pa environment.json
\(em options, keybindings, plugin declarations.
You rarely write that file by hand: you write a small
.Em config program
.Pq Go or TypeScript, against a tiny SDK ,
rook runs it, shows you the diff against what is currently applied, and
applies it when you say so.
Authoring like Pulumi, state like kubectl.
.Pp
The config directory is, in order:
the
.Fl -config Ar dir
given on the command line, else
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rook ,
else
.Pa ~/.config/rook .
Inside it rook knows these files:
.Bl -tag -width ".rook-candidate.json" -offset indent
.It Pa environment.json
The
.Em applied
graph.
Read at launch; when present it wins outright.
.It Pa config.toml
Fallback front end when no graph exists
.Pq or the graph fails to parse .
.It Pa main.go , Pa config.ts , Pa config.mts
The config program.
First hit in that order wins \(em Go beats TypeScript on a tie, by
convention rather than configuration.
.It Pa go.mod , Pa rook.ts
Support files written by onboarding
.Pq the TS SDK ships as a file beside your config, not as an npm package .
.It Pa .rook-candidate.json
Transient output of a config-program run, deleted after each check.
.El
.Pp
A directory holding only a hand-written
.Pa environment.json
and no program is perfectly legal.
Configuration is live: rook polls a content digest at 1 Hz and re-applies
on change.
.Sh THE CONFIG PROGRAM
rook runs the program from the config directory as
.Bd -literal -offset indent
go run . --out <candidate>          # main.go
npx tsx config.ts --out <candidate> # config.ts / config.mts
.Ed
.Pp
The contract is one flag: write the graph JSON to the
.Fl -out
path.
Stdout is not the graph \(em stdout and stderr are captured and shown to you
verbatim when the program fails.
A missing toolchain is reported as exactly that.
.Pp
When does it run?
On a fresh start with no config at all, rook offers onboarding
.Pq Go or TypeScript
and writes starter files \(em it does not run them yet.
After that, whenever the program's source changes
.Pq or is newer than the applied graph ,
rook runs it into a candidate, diffs, and shows the result.
.Ss Preview and apply
The diff is by node
.Em id ,
set-wise: node order and key order are not changes.
Each row is
.Ql + ,
.Ql - ,
or
.Ql ~
with the node id and a one-line detail
.Pq Ql font-size: 16 -> 20 .
A program that fails to compile or emits an unparseable graph shows as
.Em broken
with its own output \(em never as
.Dq no changes .
.Pp
Pending changes open the config side panel, unfocused, and raise an
attention.
In the panel:
.Ql j / k
move,
.Ql Enter
or
.Ql a
applies \(em the
.Em whole
diff, there is no partial apply; half a config is not a state the graph
has.
From outside:
.Ql ctl env
prints the same diff and
.Ql ctl env apply
applies it
.Pq see Xr rook-ctl 7 .
Palette commands:
.Ql config.preview ,
.Ql config.apply ,
.Ql config.edit ,
.Ql config.setup .
.Pp
Applying writes the candidate over
.Pa environment.json ;
the live reload does the rest.
.Sh THE GRAPH
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "rookEnvironment": 1,
  "nodes": [
    {"id": "opt.app.theme", "kind": "option", "scope": "app",
     "key": "theme", "value": "nocturne"},
    {"id": "leader.app", "kind": "leader", "scope": "app",
     "key": "SPACE"},
    {"id": "bind.app.p", "kind": "keybind", "scope": "app",
     "chord": "<leader>p", "command": "plugin.open"},
    {"id": "workspace:rook", "kind": "workspace", "scope": "app",
     "name": "rook", "root": "~/src/rook"},
    {"id": "plugin.hello", "kind": "plugin", "name": "hello",
     "command": ["/path/to/hello-plugin"], "load": "lazy",
     "grants": ["items.list"]}
  ]
}
.Ed
.Pp
Unknown fields and unknown keys are ignored \(em a graph from a newer SDK
degrades rather than breaks.
Node kinds rook reads:
.Bl -tag -width "keybind" -offset indent
.It Cm option
.Pq scope Ql app
One
.Ar key Ns / Ns Ar value
pair; the keys are listed below.
A
.Ql preset
option is applied first regardless of its position in the graph.
.It Cm leader
The leader key, per scope:
.Ql app
.Pq the chrome leader
or
.Ql editor
.Pq the editor's own leader .
.It Cm keybind
.Pq scope Ql app
A chord that must begin with
.Ql <leader> ,
followed by one character or
.Cm TAB , SPACE , ESC ,
bound to a registry command by name
.Pq Ql ctl commands No lists them .
Defaults are installed first; the graph rebinds.
Unknown command names are skipped silently.
.It Cm workspace
A named directory rook treats as a workspace:
.Cm name
and
.Cm root .
The palette lists it, a space launched inside it wears its name, and
worktree tooling anchors on its root.
A leading
.Ql ~/
in root expands against
.Ev $HOME .
This is the whole workspace registry \(em there is no database behind it;
worktrees are derived from git rather than declared.
.It Cm plugin
A plugin declaration \(em see
.Xr rook-plugin 7 .
.El
.Ss Option keys
Dashes and underscores are interchangeable.
Out-of-range values fall back to the default rather than erroring.
.Bl -tag -width "background-opacity" -offset indent
.It Cm font-size
Number, clamped 6\(en72.
Default 13.
.It Cm font-family
Font name.
.It Cm theme
Theme name
.Pq built-ins include Ql nocturne , Ql vscode-dark , ... .
.It Cm background-opacity
0.3\(en1.0.
.It Cm background-blur
.Ql none , blur , glass , glass-clear .
.It Cm window-padding , Cm window-padding-x , Cm window-padding-y
Points, 0\(en32.
.It Cm bell
.Ql none , visual , audible , all .
.It Cm scrollback
Lines as a number, or a size string like
.Ql 10mb ;
1 GiB ceiling.
.It Cm clipboard-write
Allow programs to write the clipboard via OSC 52
.Pq bool, or Ql allow Ns / Ns Ql deny .
.It Cm buffer-line
Per-pane buffer line:
.Ql off , multiple , always
.Pq bool accepted: true means Ql multiple .
.It Cm cursor-blink
Bool.
.It Cm editor-mode
Mode a fresh editor starts in:
.Ql normal
or
.Ql insert .
.It Cm activity-bar
Bool: the VS Code-style rail.
.It Cm explorer-auto
Bool: file tree opens with the editor.
.It Cm editor-lsp
Bool: language servers on or off.
.It Cm top-bar , Cm status-left , Cm status-right
Segment lists \(em arrays of up to 8 from:
.Ql tabs , workspace , branch , cwd , hints , hud , title .
.Ql []
reclaims the row.
.It Cm tab-style
.Ql chips , index-name , current .
.It Cm preset
A persona bundle applied before everything else:
.Ql rook
.Pq default ,
.Ql tmux-neovim ,
.Ql vscode .
Your other nodes then override on top.
.El
.Sh THE SDKS
Both SDKs build the same graph and emit byte-identical JSON; a node
re-declared later replaces the earlier one in place
.Pq same id, later value wins .
.Pp
Go
.Pq module Ql github.com/incantery/rook/sdk/rook :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
package main

import "github.com/incantery/rook/sdk/rook"

func main() {
    e := rook.New()
    e.Theme("nocturne").FontSize(14)
    e.PresetTmuxNeovim()
    e.PluginPinned("https://example.com/hello-plugin",
        "459e7f1e...", "items.list")
    e.Run()
}
.Ed
.Pp
TypeScript
.Pq Pa rook.ts No beside your config; node >= 23 or bun :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
import { env } from "./rook.ts";

const e = env();
e.theme("nocturne").fontSize(14);
e.presetTmuxNeovim();
e.pluginPinned("https://example.com/hello-plugin",
    "459e7f1e...", ["items.list"]);
e.run();
.Ed
.Pp
The surface is the option keys above as named methods, plus
.Ql leader / editorLeader ,
.Ql bind ,
.Ql workspace ,
.Ql plugin / pluginFrom / pluginPinned ,
generic
.Ql set / option
escape hatches, and the two preset bundles
.Pq expanded at emit, so the diff shows real nodes .
.Sh FILES
See
.Xr rook 1
for the full path table.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rook 1 ,
.Xr rook-ctl 7 ,
.Xr rook-plugin 7
.Sh CAVEATS
.Cm nav-yield
.Pq programs that keep ctrl-hjkl
is read from
.Pa config.toml
only; the graph has no such key yet.
.Pp
Editor-scoped keybind nodes are parsed and dropped \(em only
.Ql app Ns -scope
binds take effect today.
.Ql table
nodes and
.Ql host Ns -scope
options are carried but consumed by nothing.
.Pp
The
.Ql rookEnvironment
version integer is recorded, not enforced.
.Pp
Plugin declarations are read once at launch: adding or removing a plugin
takes a relaunch, unlike every other node kind.
.Pp
Config programs are Go or TypeScript; Python is not supported as a config
language.
